I am using the method findJobs in JobManager to iterate through all Sling jobs.

I would like to find all history jobs with a finished date before a certain date specified by a user.

First of all, there are no tests that test templates with operations, so I had to reverse engineer how should I build the template.

In the end, I created a template like this:
{code:java}
Map<String, Object> templateBefore = Map.of("<" + JobImpl.PROPERTY_FINISHED_DATE,"2026-04-03T11:38:25.360+03:00");  {code}
The template is not working though because the key is encoded before extracting the first character and the first character is no longer '<'.
{code:java}
final String key = ISO9075.encode(current.getKey());
final char firstChar = key.length() > 0 ? key.charAt(0) : 0;
final String propName;
final Operation op;
if ( firstChar == '=' ) {
    propName = key.substring(1);
    op  = Operation.EQUALS;
} else if ( firstChar == '<' ) {
    final char secondChar = key.length() > 1 ? key.charAt(1) : 0;
    if ( secondChar == '=' ) {
        op = Operation.LESS_OR_EQUALS;
        propName = key.substring(2);
    } else {
        op = Operation.LESS;
        propName = key.substring(1);
    }
}  {code}
Could you confirm the bug and if it is not a bug, share a template that can work in the scenario I described?

Thanks!

